## How these rules are enforced

| Layer | What it does |
|---|---|
| `PostToolUse` hook | Lints every file the moment it is written |
| `.claude/rules/*.md` | Path-scoped detail that loads when matching files are touched |
| `Stop` hook | Blocks the turn from ending while typecheck fails |
| `__GATE_CMD__` | The PR gate; CI runs the same script |

What no hook enforces: the load test, the leak probe, running the feature
yourself, and judgement about cost. Those live in `docs/feature-workflow.md`.

## Working agreement

- Run `__GATE_CMD__` before declaring work done. Do not disable either hook.
- Never add a lint-disable for a hard rule. If a rule is wrong, change the
  rule and its doc together, in the same PR, with the reason.
- When a rule conflicts with what you were about to write, the rule wins. Say
  so and propose the change rather than working around it.
